<% content_for :title, "Editoriall — the copy desk for humans and agents" %>

<div class="mx-auto max-w-5xl px-5 pb-20">
  <header class="flex items-end justify-between gap-6 border-b border-ink pt-8 pb-4">
    <div>
      <p class="kicker">Vol. 1 — Collaboration from the first sentence</p>
      <h1 class="mt-2 text-5xl font-bold tracking-tight sm:text-7xl"><%= wordmark(link: false) %></h1>
    </div>
    <nav class="mb-2 flex gap-4 font-mono text-[0.72rem] uppercase tracking-[0.14em]">
      <%= link_to "Sign in", new_session_path %>
      <%= link_to "Sit down", new_registration_path %>
    </nav>
  </header>

  <p class="mx-auto mt-10 max-w-3xl text-center text-2xl italic leading-snug text-ink-soft sm:text-3xl">
    An opinionated writing tool. One human in the chair. Agents on the masthead. Passes, not prompts.
  </p>

  <div class="mt-10 flex justify-center gap-3">
    <%= link_to "Open a desk", new_registration_path, class: "btn" %>
    <%= link_to "Sign in", new_session_path, class: "btn btn-ghost" %>
  </div>

  <hr class="rule mt-14">

  <section class="mt-10 grid gap-10 md:grid-cols-3">
    <article>
      <p class="kicker">01</p>
      <h2 class="mt-2 text-2xl font-semibold tracking-tight">The chair</h2>
      <p class="mt-3 leading-relaxed text-ink-soft">Someone holds the copy. Everyone else marks it. Collaboration is a desk, not a swarm of cursors. Take the chair when you mean to write. Leave it when you mean to edit.</p>
    </article>
    <article>
      <p class="kicker">02</p>
      <h2 class="mt-2 text-2xl font-semibold tracking-tight">The marks</h2>
      <p class="mt-3 leading-relaxed text-ink-soft">Notes live on the words they accuse. Quote the line. Say what is wrong, missing, or better. Humans and agents file the same kind of mark. The chair resolves them.</p>
    </article>
    <article>
      <p class="kicker">03</p>
      <h2 class="mt-2 text-2xl font-semibold tracking-tight">The pass</h2>
      <p class="mt-3 leading-relaxed text-ink-soft">Agents do not type into the live piece. They return a pass: a full revision you can read, apply, or kill. Copy, slot, research — hired onto the masthead like anyone else.</p>
    </article>
  </section>

  <section class="panel mt-16 p-8 md:p-12">
    <p class="kicker">Masthead</p>
    <h2 class="mt-2 text-3xl font-semibold tracking-tight">Built for collaboration from day one.</h2>
    <p class="mt-4 max-w-2xl leading-relaxed text-ink-soft">A new desk comes with a copy editor, a slot editor, and a researcher already seated. Your first piece is the house style. Rewrite it until the desk sounds like you, then file the next one.</p>
    <ul class="mt-8 grid gap-3 font-mono text-sm sm:grid-cols-3">
      <li class="flex items-center gap-3 border-t border-rule pt-3"><span class="avatar" style="background:#1c1914">You</span> In the chair</li>
      <li class="flex items-center gap-3 border-t border-rule pt-3"><span class="avatar" style="background:#c0392b">Co</span> Copy · agent</li>
      <li class="flex items-center gap-3 border-t border-rule pt-3"><span class="avatar" style="background:#2c4a6e">Sl</span> Slot · agent</li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <footer class="mt-16 flex items-center justify-between border-t border-ink pt-4 font-mono text-[0.68rem] uppercase tracking-[0.14em] text-ink-soft">
    <span>Editoriall</span>
    <span>Humans write. Agents pass. The chair decides.</span>
  </footer>
</div>
